course: dictionary
lesson: 3061
title: The word economic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Economic» means to do with money, trade, jobs and business in a country or area. When you meet it, look at the words next to it, because they show which part of life is being talked about. In «economic growth», the growth is about money and business, not about plants or people getting taller.
explain: Read «The economic cycle is the ups and downs of the economy: a boom is good times and a recession is bad times.» The economy is the money side of a country's life, so economic is about that money side. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "the ups and downs of the money and jobs side" still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the word can mean making a profit or giving good value. But that meaning has a better word, «economical», so when a sentence is about a country, a town or jobs, economic keeps its first meaning.
fact: Economic means to do with money, trade, jobs and business.
fact: The economy is the money side of a country's life.
fact: «Economic growth» means money and business in a country are getting bigger.
fact: «Economic crisis» means a very bad time for money and jobs, such as the 1930s, when millions lost their jobs.
fact: A recession is a bad time when businesses make and sell less, and «economic slowdown» means a recession or something close to one.
exercise: In «The economic cycle is the ups and downs of the economy», what does economic mean? | To do with plants and animals | To do with the weather | *To do with money, trade and business | To do with sport
exercise: «In the 1930s a huge economic crisis left millions without jobs.» What was the crisis about? | *Money, trade and jobs | Cooking and food | Sport and games | Music and art
exercise: Mia says economic and economical are the same. What is the best answer? | *Economic is about money and trade, and economical is usually about making a profit or good value | They are exactly the same in every sentence | Economical means very old | Economic means very hot
test: Which phrase means a bad time for money and jobs? | *Economic crisis | Economic growth | Economic reasons
test: «Countries have an exclusive economic zone up to 200 nautical miles out.» What is the zone about? | Weather forecasts | Ships' colours | *Money, fishing and minerals in the sea | Trees on the coast
exam: Which sentence best describes an economic slowdown? | Children have longer holidays | Everyone gets a pay rise and shops are full | *Many people lose their jobs and businesses make less | The sun shines all year
